{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "They spent the day preparing as though for a guest. Tobias split kindling in the yard while Mira swept the floor around the machine, careful not to let the broom come near the pivot. By noon the stove was roaring again, and the ice in the kettle had become a slow, muttering boil. Neither of them mentioned the ledger, though it lay open on the table between them through every meal, the underlined word facing the ceiling like an eye that would not close. In the afternoon Tobias built a low wall of stacked books around the base of the machine, packing the gaps with wool torn from an old blanket. \"To keep the draught off,\" he said, but Mira noticed he left one side open, the side that faced the window. When the light began to fail, he lit only a single candle and set it on the sill. The swinging arm threw a long shadow across the boards, back and forth, back and forth, steady as breathing. Mira sat with the ledger in her lap and the pencil behind her ear. She had resolved to write down everything, every hour, every change, no matter how small. Tobias took the chair beside her and wrapped his coat tighter. Outside, the valley filled with blue darkness, and the first stars came out sharp and cold above the ridge. Near midnight, the arm faltered. It did not stop. It hesitated at the top of its swing, a breath too long, as though it had heard its name called from very far away."}
